<title>USA: Inland sells stake in mine, sees Q2 gain.</title>
<headline>Inland sells stake in mine, sees Q2 gain.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inland Steel Industries Inc said Monday it completed the sale of its 15 percent interest in the Wabush Iron Ore mine to a subsidiary of Cleveland-Cliffs Inc, the mine's managing agent.</p>
<p>The sale resulted in a pretax gain of $9 million, or $0.11 a share, to be recognized in Inland's second quarter ended June 30.</p>
<p>The sale is &quot;another step in our efforts to lower fixed costs and maintain the proper balance between our iron ore supplies and needs,&quot; said Inland Steel President Dale Wiersbe, in a news release.</p>
<p>			 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
